{"step": 8, "t": 1791709560.3, "kind": "final_answer", "content": "**Dataset** \u2013 1\u202f000 rows, 66 engineered features (after dropping *id* and *nickname*); target *vibe_score_0_100* is a 101\u2011class classification problem with roughly uniform class distribution.  \n\n**Model comparison (5\u2011fold CV, accuracy)**  \n\n| Rank | Model               | Accuracy |\n|------|---------------------|----------|\n| 1    | random_forest       | 0.015 |\n| 2    | gradient_boosting   | 0.015 |\n| 3    | logistic_regression | 0.013 |\n| 4    | decision_tree       | 0.012 |\n| 5    | knn                 | 0.011 |\n\n**Recommended baseline** \u2013 **Random Forest** (top accuracy). It handles mixed categorical/numeric data well, is robust to over\u2011fitting with limited samples, and automatically captures non\u2011linear interactions among the many features.  \n\n**Caveat** \u2013 With 101 balanced classes and only 1\u202f000 examples, even the best baseline yields very low accuracy; more data or a reformulated target (e.g., grouping scores) will be needed for a useful predictive model.", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "tokens": 2331}
